                "source_context": "As traditional Marian Catholic priests grew old and died, the Catholic faith in England faced extinction. William Allen founded Douai College in Spanish-controlled Flanders to educate a new generation of missionary priests, transforming passive English Catholicism into an active Counter-Reformation movement. **Hinge Question:** How did the arrival of seminary priests from Douai transform the Elizabethan government's perception of Catholic subjects from harmless dissenters into active traitors?"
